  "description": "My property (76D Clapham Common Northside) has a small garden which backs onto Meteor street. The length of the garden from the property to the rear boundary wall with Meteor Street is approximately 3.5m. The garden contains two trees as outlined in the sketch plan submitted with this application (NB. Not too scale). Due to their proximity to my flat, these require regular pruning (every year) in order to protect the property from any root damage (this was a recommendation of the surveyor's report when I bought the property in 2012) and also to prevent excessive shading in the garden and blocking of light into the first floor of my flat, and the flat above mine (76C). The trees are not subject to any Tree Preservation Orders but my property is located within a conservation area, hence why I always have to apply for permission to carry out the works listed below. I have never been refused permission for this work previously. Laburnum (T1) - crown reduction to about 70% (eg. by about 1-1.5m) English Walnut (T2) - crown reduction to about 70% (eg. by about 3m) and crown thinning of about 30%",
